    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "With a pleasing sylvan aspect to the front overlooking the countryside to Carrickgollogan Hill and enjoying an enviable all day sunny southwest orientation to delightful rear gardens, 8 Glen View is situated in a tranquil enclave within a leisurely stroll of Enniskerry Village.  Presented in excellent condition throughout and tastefully appointed with a high-quality specification, the natural light filled and airy interiors extend to c.210 m2   (2,260 sq ft). This impressive double bay fronted B rated detached 4 double bedroom family home offers well planned free flowing accommodation comprise rooms of good dimensions with feature high ceilings.\r\nEnniskerry is famous for its natural beauty and Victorian architecture, making it a popular filming location. Centered around a \"village triangle\" featuring a 19th-century clock tower, local amenities include artisan boutiques, cafes and bistros. A haven for outdoor recreation, from championship golf courses to mountain biking trails, and the world-renowned Powerscourt House and Estate is immediately adjacent to the Village.\r\nThere are excellent local primary schools and short commutes to highly regarded secondary schools. Transport to the city is easily accessible via N11/M50 or route 44 Dublin Bus, and Luas Green line from Dundrum."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch with tiled floor\r\nSpacious Reception Hall\r\n4.88m x 4.36m\t\twith solid Maple flooring, bespoke built-in display unit, decorative radiator cabinet and recessed lighting.  Valuable understairs storage. Suitable for integration with Kitchen/dining area. \r\n\r\nGuest Cloakroom\r\nContemporary white suite incorporating w.c. and w.h.b. in vanity unit and wall mirror.  Tiled walls to dado level and tiled floor.\r\n\r\nDrawing Room\r\n8.9m x 4.3m \twith feature dual aspect.  Fine marble fireplace with marble hearth and fitted with Barbas solid fuel fire. Bay window. Recessed lighting. Decorative radiator cabinets. French doors to gardens.\r\n\r\nSitting Room\r\n4.7m x 3.4m \t\twith bay window, marble fireplace with marble hearth and fitted with electric coal effect fire. Recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining\r\nExtensive open plan area:\r\nKitchen\r\n4.96m x 3.04m \t\tsuperbly fitted with stylish range of units with stainless steel detail finished  with granite work tops and uprights and tiling surround.  Quality appliances included Samsung American style fridge/freezer and SMEG electric dual range cooker combined with 6 place gas burner hob along with Siemens dishwasher.  Tiled floor.  Recessed lighting.\r\n\r\n                                                    OPENING TO:\r\nDining Area\r\n4.10m x 2.98m  \t\twith tiled floor. French doors to gardens and patio.\r\n\r\nUtility room\r\n1.63m x 1.56m \t\twith fitted units.  Samsung washing machine and Hot Point dryer. (Hot water and heating provided by condensing gas boiler with zoned heating \r\ncontrols)\r\n\r\n Tiled floor. Door to gardens.\r\n\r\nAttractive staircase to spacious LANDING.  Hot Press with insulated cylinder and fitted with timer.\r\nMaster Bedroom 1\r\n5.3m x 4.64m \t\twith wall to wall built-in wardrobes and vanity unit.  Decorative radiator cabinet.  Stunning views of Enniskerry Glen and Carrickgollogan Hill.\r\n\r\nBathroom En Suite\r\n2.45m x 2.3m   \t\tContemporary white suite incorporating bath with shower attachment. Power tiled shower, w.h.b. in vanity unit, wall mirror, w.c. and heated towel rail.  Window.  Fully tiled walls and floor.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\n4.28m x 3.98m\r\n\r\nShower Room En Suite\r\n2.45m x 2.3m   \tContemporary white suite incorporating tiled power shower, w.b. in vanity unit, w.c. and wall mirror.  Tiled walls to dado level and tiled floor.  Window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\n4.3m x 3.98m\t\twith fitted wardrobes, book shelves, study desk and built-in display unit.  Super views to the coast and Enniskerry Glen. Recessed lights.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\n4.3m x 4.3m \t\twith fitted wardrobes and bed. Drop down desk.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom\r\n2.9m x 2.16m  \t White period style suite comprising bath with tiled surround, fitted power shower, pedestal w.h.b. and w.c.  Heated towel rail and mirror door medicine cabinet.  Tiled floor and walls to dado level. Window.\r\n\r\nOUTSIDE\r\nTo the front the cobblelock driveway offers generous front of house off street car parking. 2 gated side entrances give access to the landscaped rear garden measuring 24m long by 14.9m wide. The generous cobblelock patio and feature raised timber deck with curved brick frontage give way to the rolling lawn, raised brick fronted flower beds and herbaceous borders.  There are illuminated Indian Sandstone steps leading to the elevated viewing area. The garden storage shed is clad with wisteria and clematis. There is a host of mature trees and specimen shrubs. This peaceful and tranquil setting enjoys a very private aspect and an all day sunny southwest orientation. With external lighting and outdoor infrared heater affixed to patio wall area."
      },
      {
